  "limitations": [
    "Single-view TRELLIS reconstruction from one concept: hands are fused 'mitten' shapes (a thumb and two or three joined fingers), and the face is soft, with smeared eye sockets.",
    "All four concepts were painted over the line soldier's reference body, so the belt, the pouch on the left hip and the laced boots repeat across the roster.",
    "TRELLIS invented a near-black back on every seed; the back is a projected rear-view concept, blended into the reconstructed texture at the sides, with the nearest painted colour carried into a few unpainted back pixels.",
    "Roughness, metalness and ambient occlusion are derived from colour inside declared regions and a Cycles bake, not measured PBR or hand-painted masks.",
    "Linear blend skinning with shoulder, hip and knee helpers: creases stretch up to about 2x at the 99.5th percentile in combat frames, and single edges up to about 8x at armpit, elbow and hip creases. Decimation slivers under 8 mm are collapsed first.",
    "Weapons and the quiver are low-poly Blender-authored meshes with flat painted colour, not reconstructed from a concept.",
    "Procedural clips authored in Blender (no motion capture), no root motion. The game scales the captain x1.2 and the bosses x1.7 as the procedural figures were; their Run is authored at the simulation speed divided by that scale.",
    "Re-cooking is not guaranteed to be byte-reproducible: MikkTSpace tangents can round differently on a few vertices, and Blender's smart UV project can lay out the item atlas differently between runs.",
    "The short shoulder cape was reconstructed fused to the upper arms; a weight ramp hands it from the arms to the chest, so it stretches a little when the bow is raised instead of tearing.",
